    skos:definition '''{"node": {
    "platformclass": "vessel at fixed position",
    "notes": "Ocean Weather ship M(ike), still operating at the eastern margin of the Norwegian sea deep basin where a branch of the Atlantic current is entering the area. At 66N, 2E. Recording since October 1948 can present longest existing homogenous time series from the deep ocean.   Ship is currently operated by the Norwegian Meterological Institute (DNMI) and the hydrographic programme is carried out by the Geophysical Institute, Univ of Bergen."
}}'''@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:C17::74D7'^^xsd:string .
